    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d464">

                <pb facs="0495" n="395" sameAs="frus:frus1920v03/pg395"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">760c.61/266</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Under Secretary of State</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Davis</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-08-27"><hi rendition="#italic">August 27,
                        1920</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: The British Chargé delivered
                    to me the attached note,<anchor n="24" xml:id="d464-f1"/> to which I replied
                    that as this Government has not ratified the treaty, we could not very well take
                    the measures indicated specifically to force compliance with the Treaty, but
                    that we are concerned about the situation in Dantzig and would probably send a
                    ship to Dantzig for the purpose of protecting American rights, <pb facs="0496"
                        n="396" xml:id="pg396"/> property and interests. He indicated that the
                    effect was the principal thing desired, and that this would no doubt accomplish
                    that purpose.</p>
                <p>If you concur, I suggest that you request the Secretary of the Navy to take the
                    action indicated.<anchor n="25" xml:id="d464-f2"/></p>
                <closer><signed>N[<hi rendition="#small-caps">orman</hi>] H. D[<hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">avis</hi>]</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
